From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:04:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 30/31] feat(midea): report tankwatch water tank estimates as
 consumables

Reads /userdata/tankwatch/state.json (written by the tankwatch daemon on
the robot) and exposes the clean tank (water left) and the dirty tank
(space left) as percent consumables. The parsed file is cached by mtime
and size; a missing, unreadable, malformed or version != 1 file means no
estimate. Resetting a consumable creates the flag file
/tmp/tankwatch.reset-clean or /tmp/tankwatch.reset-dirty, which the
daemon picks up.

The capability is only registered on the J15 Pro Ultra when the state
file exists at startup.

